# Dev tooling follow-up

- Align `thread view --json` with `docs/debugging.md`'s untruncated JSON contract.
  `tools/mf/src/commands/thread/chat-view.ts` still clips text unless `--full` is
  also passed. Reproduce with a handoff seed and compare `thread view --json` against
  `thread view --full --json`.

- Give the dev log directory and Nitro's watcher exclusion one source of truth.
  `apps/server/nitro.config.ts` builds its own `<repo>/logs/**` exclusion while
  `lib/dev-env.ts` `resolveDevLogDir` resolves `LOG_DIR` (honoring any absolute
  override); moving one without the other lets JSONL mirror writes rebuild Nitro
  and orphan in-flight replies. Export one typed dev-runtime path both consume.

- Name a worktree's database from its checkout path instead of its branch. Ports already
  come from the path; the database is the last thing tied to the branch, which is why a
  stack must be restarted after its worktree switches branch (`session-identity.ts`,
  `resolveWorktreeDatabaseName` in `lib/dev-env.ts`). Changing it reruns the full DB suite.
